cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Amortized probabilistic retrieval of atmospheric CO2 from OCO-2 spectra:
  code and reproduction pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the paper and this software record.
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/acallesalda/oco2-amortized-uq"
version: v1.0.1
date-released: "2026-09-09"
abstract: >-
  Training and evaluation code for amortized probabilistic retrieval of atmospheric CO2
  from OCO-2 spectra. A convolutional-transformer network maps a three-band spectrum to a
  predictive distribution over column-average CO2, the 20-level CO2 profile, or the four
  near-surface levels; uncertainty is obtained either from a last-layer Laplace
  approximation or from a conditional rational-quadratic spline normalizing flow, and both
  are compared against the operational ACOS L2FP retrieval on held-out geophysical scenes
  and on two held-out months. Includes the data-preparation pipelines, the six trainers,
  the selected hyperparameters, the GPU scoring pass, and the scripts that regenerate every
  table and figure in the accompanying paper.
keywords:
  - OCO-2
  - remote sensing
  - atmospheric CO2 retrieval
  - uncertainty quantification
  - normalizing flows
  - Laplace approximation
  - amortized inference
  - deep learning

